# OTC release manifest (issue #94).
#
# One release per line, OLDEST FIRST, tab-separated:
#
#   <version>	<sha256 of scripts/updates/<version>.sh>	<description>
#
# A device stores the version it is on in /etc/otc/version and applies every
# script *after* that one, in this order, to reach the newest. That is what
# makes an update incremental: a device two releases behind runs two
# scripts, not a reinstall.
#
# Rules for anything added here:
#
#   1. Every script MUST be idempotent. A device with no /etc/otc/version
#      (every install made before this feature existed) starts from the
#      beginning and runs all of them, so re-running a script must be a
#      no-op rather than an error - and must never destroy data. Schema
#      changes are ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS / CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS,
#      never DROP, never a re-import of db.sql.
#   2. A script only carries what is specific to its release. Refreshing
#      the binary is common to every update and is done once at the end by
#      scripts/update.sh - don't repeat it here.
#   3. The sha256 is checked before the script is run as root. Regenerate
#      it whenever the script changes:
#        shasum -a 256 scripts/updates/<version>.sh
#
1	7b85090a127fcea7cb3c9b6eef5ad1dd28bcdcde5f3088147626c4ee855318f7	Schema catch-up for installs made before in-place updates existed
